content.text:
Now background rewrite. We'll replace the entire drawBackground function. Need ensure it uses hash2 and camera. We'll write a natural forest floor with patches, grass, pebbles, roots, mushrooms, fireflies. No grid.

Let's design carefully:

```
function drawBackground() {
  const g = ctx.createLinearGradient(0, 0, 0, H);
  g.addColorStop(0, '#171a12');
  g.addColorStop(0.52, '#10130d');
  g.addColorStop(1, '#080a07');
  ctx.fillStyle = g; fillRect.

  const halfW... left/right/top/bottom
  ctx.save(); applyCamera();

  // warm torchlight around player
  const glow = radial(player.x, player.y, 20, 620);
  glow.addColorStop(0,'rgba(208,168,96,0.10)');
  glow.addColorStop(0.55,'rgba(120,100,60,0.04)');
  glow.addColorStop(1,'rgba(0,0,0,0)');
  fill.

  // soft moss patches: large radial gradients at hash points? Could be expensive. Use tile 240 with 2-3 gradients visible. We can draw large ellipses with low alpha.
  const patch = 260;
  for tx... for ty... h=hash2; if h<0.5:
    ctx.fillStyle = h<0.25 ? 'rgba(60,74,42,0.12)' : 'rgba(78,64,44,0.10)';
    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.ellipse(px,py, 80+h*70, 46+h*40, h*TAU,0,TAU); ctx.fill();

  // small details tile 90:
    const h = hash2(tx+3, ty+7)
    if h<0.10: grass tuft (3 blades) stroke rgba(110,130,75,0.20)
    else if h<0.16: pebbles (2 ellipses) fill rgba(130,120,100,0.16)
    else if h<0.20: root: bezier stroke rgba(90,70,50,0.15)
    else if h<0.23: mushroom: stem + cap rgba(160,110,70,0.22)
    else if h<0.26: dirt patch small ellipse rgba(70,60,42,0.15)
  // fireflies:
  for i 0..18: use hash2(i,1) and time; x = left + ((hash*width + sin(t*...)) mod width); y...; fill gold alpha 0.15.
  ctx.restore();
}
```
Need to avoid too many draw calls; tile 90 over 1280x720/1.13 => ~15x9 =135 tiles, fine. Patch tile 260 ~7x5=35. Fireflies 18. Good.

Use `run.time` for fireflies; title uses ambient. In gameplay, `run.time` exists. Good.

Maybe add a subtle diagonal light shaft? Not necessary.

